WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.490
- Well hey, let's bring
in the other judges--

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:04.790
- No, let's just keep
it you and I, I'm happy.

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:07.390
- We have to bring them
in, they've been waiting.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:08.571
- I'm not ready!

00:00:08.571 --> 00:00:09.880
(laughs)

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:10.713
- Oh my gosh!

00:00:10.713 --> 00:00:12.123
- Honey, the blue shirt.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.295
- [Terry] I didn't wanna see that.

00:00:15.295 --> 00:00:16.920
- [Sofia] What's going on?

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.750
- (mumbles) a horror movie.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.741
- I love you so much right now, oh my God.

00:00:21.741 --> 00:00:22.920
- What are you doing?

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.910
- You wanna know honestly
what I'm doing, Simon?

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.173
- I have a feeling and
I don't wanna see it.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:30.540
- You inspired me, Simon,

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.280
that you were able to
(microphone cuts out).

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.050
Well, here's what it is.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:37.166
Terry Crews is the consummate host,

00:00:37.166 --> 00:00:38.530
good friend and everything.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:41.020
What is he known for
besides hosting our show?

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.870
- Having huge pecs.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:44.819
- And able to control them, right?

00:00:44.819 --> 00:00:46.090
(laughs)

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:47.420
And you can do it now, too, right?

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:49.690
- I can do it now, as well, yep.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.060
- [Howie] Let's see.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:52.690
- Um, hang on, I don't know if they show.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:53.940
Okay, hang on one second.

00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:57.053
- There it is, yes, yes.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:00:59.940
- I mean it's not as good as you, Terry,

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:00.910
but I'm getting there.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:01.743
- No, it's--

00:01:01.743 --> 00:01:04.860
- Hey, guys, I've been practicing at home.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.197
I'm not there yet, but--

00:01:07.116 --> 00:01:08.116
- Oh my God!

00:01:09.207 --> 00:01:10.185
- Look.

00:01:10.185 --> 00:01:12.030
(laughs)

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.670
Edit the show you can edit
out the strings and everything

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.887
so I look more talented, no?

00:01:16.887 --> 00:01:19.485
- You know what, Howie, you
know what you look like?

00:01:19.485 --> 00:01:21.950
You know when you get one of
these really bad auditions

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:24.280
on the show and all you're
thinking is how quickly

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:26.133
can I get you off the stage?

00:01:27.442 --> 00:01:30.330
We're in that kind of place right now.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:32.240
- Are you giving me a red buzzer?

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:34.430
- Yes, millions of them.

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:35.830
- Hey Sofia, how you doin'?

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:37.640
- How are you, Kelly?

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.455
Hi everybody!

00:01:39.455 --> 00:01:41.020
- (mumbles) Sofia!

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:43.303
- Heidi, gosh that eye
makeup I'm in love with,

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:45.056
that is amazing.

00:01:45.056 --> 00:01:46.285
- Amazing!

00:01:46.285 --> 00:01:47.118
- Hi!

00:01:47.118 --> 00:01:47.968
- [Simon] Where is Heidi?

00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:48.801
- Hi!

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:50.970
- [Kelly] She's on the other,
I had to flip the screen,

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:53.210
yeah, there's a lot of us.
It's a large Zoom call.

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:55.269
- Oh okay.

00:01:55.269 --> 00:01:56.387
Hi Heidi!

00:01:56.387 --> 00:01:57.337
- Hi!

00:01:57.337 --> 00:01:58.250
- Everybody out there
please welcome Howie Mandel,

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:02.537
Heidi Klum, Sofia Vergara, and
the host of AGT, Terry Crews.

00:02:02.537 --> 00:02:03.370
- Hey, hey.

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:05.500
- All right, y'all, so I'm
gonna start with Howie,

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.053
naked boy number one.

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:11.430
Have the rest of these guys apologized

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:15.117
for not taking your concern
about germs seriously?

00:02:15.117 --> 00:02:15.989
(laughs)

00:02:15.989 --> 00:02:16.840
- Oh, my gosh.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.293
No, no.

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:22.363
Some people call it a
pandemic, I call it told ya.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:24.600
(laughs)

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:25.920
No, they haven't apologized.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.240
I don't want an apology.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.563
I mean all kidding aside,

00:02:31.831 --> 00:02:32.664
this is the nightmare

00:02:32.664 --> 00:02:35.940
I've lived in my own mind for
the last 64 years of my life

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:38.240
and now it was nice to
wake up and find out

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:39.120
it was only a nightmare.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.340
Now every day I'm waking
up and finding out

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.110
you're all in the nightmare with me.

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:45.192
- We're all in it with you, Howie.

00:02:45.192 --> 00:02:46.312
- [Kelly] Definitely scary.

00:02:46.312 --> 00:02:47.145
- There you are.

00:02:47.145 --> 00:02:48.133
Hi, Heidi!

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:49.122
- Hi!

00:02:49.122 --> 00:02:49.955
- You look great!

00:02:49.955 --> 00:02:52.530
- I know I love her eye
makeup and her hair.

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:54.992
I'm just like what, okay.

00:02:54.992 --> 00:02:58.590
So Heidi, actually that's
kind of a good segue

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:00.420
because you had your
own COVID scare, right?

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:01.670
You're doing well now, right?

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:05.040
- I'm fine, I never had it
but you know at the time

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.010
when it just kind of hit America

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:10.340
and when it hit Los Angeles,
I all of the sudden got sick.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:13.720
I came to set and I had
a fever, I had a cough,

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:16.210
I wasn't feeling good, you know
when you have your body ache

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:20.520
everywhere and I got there and
I told someone immediately.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.370
I was like I'm not
feeling good and you know

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:24.760
there's this corona thing going around

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.770
and immediately they had the
medic there coming to see

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.210
how high my fever was and
they dismissed me immediately

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.150
and send me home.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:35.720
and thankfully I never had it and yeah,

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:38.070
I guess everyone did the right
thing for sending me home,

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:40.450
but that's why you know

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:43.370
Terry got to come and sit in
my seat which was, I'm sure,

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:45.101
so much fun for all you guys.

00:03:45.101 --> 00:03:46.850
- By the way, Sofia was thrilled.

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:47.870
(laughs)

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:50.525
- No, Heidi, I need you.

00:03:50.525 --> 00:03:51.358
- I miss you guys so much though.

00:03:51.358 --> 00:03:54.750
It was very strange to leave
because I'm very German.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.470
I'm always very on time, I do as I'm told

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:00.500
and I've never really been
sick and been sent home,

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:01.880
so I felt so bizarre.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:03.527
But it was such a--

00:04:03.527 --> 00:04:05.330
- You know honestly,
I never told you this,

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:07.480
Sofia said look, I think she should leave

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.882
for the whole season.

00:04:08.882 --> 00:04:09.715
(laughs)

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:10.912
- No, I didn't!

00:04:10.912 --> 00:04:11.745
(laughs)

00:04:11.745 --> 00:04:13.230
- You can't take it back now.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.063
- [Terry] Oh!

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:17.190
- [Kelly] But you still
found a socially distant way

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.490
to get your hair done?

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:21.320
And I just wanna say, what the hell?

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.863
This photo is so hot.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:27.910
- I mean I have to tell
you know we have someone

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:31.580
in the family who has
(people talking over speaker)

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:35.680
immune disease, so
we've been super careful

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:38.570
from the very beginning
like not going out,

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:41.020
like washing everything
because when you have someone

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:43.930
around you with an auto-immune disease,

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:45.780
it's like extra on high alert.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:48.450
So I never really, I
haven't really seen anybody,

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:51.770
gone anywhere, done anything,
but you know we were like,

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:54.850
okay we have to do this super
proper, with the umbrella.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.640
We have all the masks on and everything,

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:57.473
just do the highlights.

00:04:57.473 --> 00:04:59.540
I mean I did all the
washing and everything else,

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:01.630
but he just came by and
did a few highlights

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.320
because I'm not a real blonde.

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:04.170
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.003
So it was like.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:09.623
- I hear you on the auto-immune thing,

00:05:09.623 --> 00:05:11.170
that is why I was so scared.

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:13.890
I have an auto-immune
disease, so I was like what?

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:16.340
And I freaked out, so I feel you on that.

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:18.440
And I love the photo.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:21.112
Forget the umbrella, no one's
looking at the damn umbrella.

00:05:21.112 --> 00:05:21.945
(laughs)

00:05:21.945 --> 00:05:22.962
- Exactly.

00:05:22.962 --> 00:05:25.272
- Well, I didn't wanna get
my outfit all messed up.

00:05:25.272 --> 00:05:26.630
You know how that is when
you get a little bleach.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:29.400
- Girl, if I was rockin'
what you and Sofia had,

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:32.250
I'd be walkin' around naked
in the frozen food section.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:33.941
(laughs)

00:05:33.941 --> 00:05:35.910
I was like I mean it's a beautiful thing,

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:37.420
God had great (mumbles) when He made--

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:38.253
- That is funny, that is funny.

00:05:41.882 --> 00:05:42.715
- I was just like, wow.

00:05:42.715 --> 00:05:44.450
Wait, Sofia, so is it true your husband,

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:45.730
this is one of my favorite things.

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:49.010
Your husband, Joe, holds a
Dungeons and Dragons club

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:49.843
in your house?

00:05:49.843 --> 00:05:53.190
I mean these photos and
once I heard about this,

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:54.023
I actually--

00:05:54.023 --> 00:05:54.856
- Do you play?

00:05:54.856 --> 00:05:55.689
Do you play this?

00:05:55.689 --> 00:05:57.120
- I want to.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.610
I'm such a nerd alert.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:01.770
I literally went down a little
rabbit hole of watching it

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:04.000
on YouTube of him talking
about who's come in and out

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.880
of the game and it's the
most random group of people.

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:08.713
So this is all true?

00:06:08.713 --> 00:06:11.490
- It's super weird, they're really weird.

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:12.323
(laughs)

00:06:12.323 --> 00:06:16.080
But (laughter over speaker)
that he comes and do it here

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:19.870
in the house, I mean now
that they are in quarantine,

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:22.350
they're doing it on Zoom.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:24.160
So they have still been playing.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:26.280
It's crazy 'cause they
can do something this game

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:30.250
for like six, seven hours
and they sing, they clap,

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:32.939
I don't know what
they're doing down there.

00:06:32.939 --> 00:06:35.430
It's like something really
weird that I can't understand,

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:37.200
but it sounds fun.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.640
- You know most people who
play Dungeons and Dragons

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:42.704
don't even meet pretty
girls, to marry one.

00:06:42.704 --> 00:06:44.650
(laughs)

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:47.200
- I was like I love that
you ended up with a guy

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:48.823
that plays Dungeons and Dragons.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:53.410
- Joe is a complete
nerd, I always tell him

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:55.700
that he's trapped in the wrong body.

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:58.320
It's like they put a nerd in this body

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:01.200
and it doesn't make any sense to me.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:04.480
- My man, he's like me,
he's right there with me.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:05.921
(laughs)

00:07:05.921 --> 00:07:07.500
I'm gonna play with him, I'm telling you,

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:09.490
we're gonna do Dungeons
and Dragons together.

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:10.490
I love it.

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:11.390
- Oh you have to.

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:13.170
Kelly and you can come, too.

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:14.760
- Oh, it looks like a man's club,

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:15.890
it looks like Little Rascals,

00:07:15.890 --> 00:07:17.601
like women aren't invited, but--

00:07:17.601 --> 00:07:18.732
(laughs)

00:07:18.732 --> 00:07:20.700
- No, no, sometimes there's been,

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:24.060
no, there have been girls
playing here many times.

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:26.210
I mean it's a small percentage,

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:28.400
but yes, they do come and play here.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:30.650
- I (mumbles) like in the lou.

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:31.983
- Okay, so wait, Howie.

00:07:32.872 --> 00:07:36.830
You just actually celebrated
your 40th wedding anniversary

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:38.330
in lockdown, did y'all
do anything special?

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:40.270
'Cause I remember your birthday
you brought an elephant in

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:42.730
for her, so, or for her birthday.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:45.030
- Um, did I do anything special?

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:49.543
Yes, I took her to the
guest room. (laughs)

00:07:53.062 --> 00:07:53.895
- That's exciting.

00:07:53.895 --> 00:07:55.920
- And what happened there?

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:57.020
- What happened?

00:07:57.020 --> 00:07:58.590
- Yeah I know, were you
christening the house

00:07:58.590 --> 00:07:59.630
or what's happening?

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:00.970
(laughs)

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:03.050
- We've christened it,
we've been here for years

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:04.570
and decades and decades.

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:09.570
You know in quarantine,
there were no surprises.

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:14.190
It's just we said we wanna
redo our vows and she came up

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:17.641
with one vow and then her
vow was enough already.

00:08:17.641 --> 00:08:19.724
(laughs)

00:08:21.661 --> 00:08:23.361
- Oh, she doesn't mean that.

00:08:23.361 --> 00:08:24.230
- Oh my gosh.

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:27.090
Wait, so okay, Sofia,
you're the newest judge,

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:28.640
so what kind of acts are you liking?

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:30.690
What are you digging about the show?

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:33.760
- You know what, I was
having such a great time.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:37.180
We had to stop because of
all the virus situation,

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:39.000
but I was having such a great time.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:43.062
I mean it was better than
I thought it was gonna be.

00:08:43.062 --> 00:08:46.530
I loved everybody, I think
we all have gotten along

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:47.680
from the beginning.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:52.290
The being there in the stage,
the contestants, everything.

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:55.760
I mean I am very lucky to
be part of this group now.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:56.593
- Oh, that's cool.

00:08:56.593 --> 00:08:58.830
I know that's what I love about
being part of "The Voice."

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:01.400
I love when I love going to work.

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:02.910
You know you love when
you love going to work

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:04.750
and showing up and everybody's cool and--

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:08.410
- Kelly, you can't talk about
the opposition, darling.

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:10.702
- Oh, what?

00:09:10.702 --> 00:09:11.535
Opposition?

00:09:11.535 --> 00:09:12.368
- The opposition, you know you're like

00:09:12.368 --> 00:09:14.550
our opposition, "The Voice."

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:17.130
- Oh, wait, but we're not
even on at the same time.

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:20.450
- It doesn't matter, it's
still kind of competition, so--

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.769
- Being very competitive,
Mr. Simon Cowell.

00:09:22.769 --> 00:09:24.736
(laughs)

00:09:24.736 --> 00:09:26.830
- [Simon] Let me just
say bad things about it.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:29.078
- Wait, we're not even
on at the same time.

00:09:29.078 --> 00:09:30.126
(laughs)

00:09:30.126 --> 00:09:32.884
- It doesn't matter, you
exist, it happens there.

00:09:32.884 --> 00:09:35.497
- [Kelly] Okay, okay,
good answer, good answer.

00:09:35.497 --> 00:09:38.067
♪ And the mother really shows herself ♪

00:09:38.067 --> 00:09:40.696
♪ Everything will be all right ♪

00:09:40.696 --> 00:09:43.068
♪ As she steps in rhythm ♪

00:09:43.068 --> 00:09:44.966
♪ To the sounds of the sidewalk ♪

00:09:44.966 --> 00:09:46.108
♪ As she steps in ♪

00:09:46.108 --> 00:09:49.417
♪ To the sounds of the sidewalk ♪

00:09:49.417 --> 00:09:51.550
(cheering)

00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:56.550
- What they did today has moved
me to this point right now.

00:09:57.668 --> 00:09:59.918
(cheering)

00:10:02.075 --> 00:10:03.060
- Hey y'all, I'm back with the team

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:06.050
of "America's Got Talent,"
Simon Cowell, Howie Mandel,

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:09.350
Heidi Klum, Sofia
Vergara, and Terry Crews.

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:11.750
All right, so Terry, you
used your golden buzzer

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:14.210
for the Voices of Our City choir.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:15.760
What did you love about them?

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:16.760
- Oh my God.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:20.630
First of all, the fact that
here we had a homeless choir

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:22.290
who came up from San Diego.

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:25.800
They wrote their own music,
they did their own things,

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:29.690
it was absolutely, it just
moved me beyond belief.

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:34.690
I was in tears and I knew
as soon as I saw them

00:10:34.770 --> 00:10:35.960
that I had to give it.

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:40.310
I just rushed the stage
because the opportunity

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:44.660
that each one of these men
and women took was a risk.

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:48.630
You know they've been cast
away, they've been marginalized

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:51.920
for so long and to get the
confidence to get up there

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:54.800
and try something like
this, I had to reward 'em

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:58.700
and let me tell you,
they were outstanding.

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:01.350
One of my best, best things
I've ever done in my life.

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:04.360
And it's like that for
all our golden buzzers.

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:05.830
- I love the golden buzzer.

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:08.610
Well, Heidi, who did you
pick for your golden buzzer?

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:11.450
- Mine was for Christina
Rae, she's a singer.

00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:13.660
I fell in love with her immediately

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:17.120
and she also has the most
heart-wrenching story,

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:22.070
but I always go with my gut
instinct and I just loved her

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:24.660
and I loved her performance,
I loved her voice.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:27.480
And I don't know, maybe it's
gonna be my golden buzzer

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:29.363
who's gonna win it all this time.

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:32.320
- Kelly, technically I think she might be

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:34.670
one of the best singers
we've ever had on the show.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:35.503
- [Terry] Yes.

00:11:35.503 --> 00:11:36.490
- Really?

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:38.223
- Yeah, honest to God.

00:11:38.223 --> 00:11:40.510
Have you watched that movie,
"Twenty Feet from Stardom"?

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:42.297
- Yeah, with Darlene Love, yeah.

00:11:42.297 --> 00:11:46.357
- Okay, she's like one
of those great singers

00:11:46.357 --> 00:11:50.555
and she hasn't been given a
shot yet, but I mean her voice

00:11:50.555 --> 00:11:52.927
is off the chart, this girl.

00:11:52.927 --> 00:11:54.070
- Oh, that's exciting!

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:57.070
I love hearing, I love
people in their element

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:58.860
just really nailin' it in what they do,

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.020
that's so (microphone cuts out).

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:02.120
Well, Simon who did you
use your golden buzzer for?

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:05.254
- Well, I actually gave my
golden buzzer to some dancers

00:12:05.254 --> 00:12:09.587
and look, I'm not a dance
expert, believe it or not.

00:12:10.478 --> 00:12:13.580
(laughs) It'd be like me
giving a golden buzzer

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:15.040
to a fashion designer,

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:17.920
you know it's like not really my thing.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:21.240
But and a bit like what Terry was saying,

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:24.984
you know their story often
has a lot to do with it

00:12:24.984 --> 00:12:26.545
and there was something about these guys

00:12:26.545 --> 00:12:28.960
and they were talking to
me and I could see how much

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:32.333
it meant to them and then I
was feeding off the audience.

00:12:33.295 --> 00:12:34.780
And you don't think
about it in the moment,

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:38.003
it's just like you just wanna
give them that extra boost.

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:42.610
I've got a feeling that they
might be in the top three

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:44.160
at the end, these guys.

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:45.020
- Wow.

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:47.660
- One of those guys threw his shoe on.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:50.003
How do you throw your shoe on?

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:52.450
Not off, on!

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:55.487
And that's how there was a
miracle, I was like (laughs).

00:12:57.030 --> 00:12:59.460
- So wait, Howie, who did you
use your golden buzzer on?

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:01.340
- Okay, mine's the only
one that hasn't aired yet

00:13:01.340 --> 00:13:03.430
and I gotta tell you something,
I've been on the show

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:06.420
and I keep mentioning this
ad nauseum for like 11 years,

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:09.370
this is the first time that
I've pressed the golden buzzer

00:13:09.370 --> 00:13:12.760
for something that has never
graced the stages of AGT.

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:16.780
It's not a singer, it's not a
magician, it's not a dancer,

00:13:16.780 --> 00:13:20.089
it's not music, it's something
you've never seen on AGT,

00:13:20.089 --> 00:13:21.970
so (microphone cuts out).

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:23.963
- Howie, I've seen it in the cut.

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:30.710
This person is phenomenal and
actually it was good then,

00:13:30.710 --> 00:13:31.980
it's even better now.

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:33.124
- Wow!

00:13:33.124 --> 00:13:35.160
- I can't even wait to watch this now.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:37.606
- I know, I'm like this is--

00:13:37.606 --> 00:13:40.127
- You've set this up so well,
I can't wait to see this now.

00:13:40.127 --> 00:13:42.280
- I know it's like the worst tease.

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:44.500
I'm like, okay, cool, I got to wait.

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:46.310
So wait, Sofia, this is
your first time to use

00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:47.143
your golden buzzer.

00:13:47.143 --> 00:13:48.230
Who was your choice?

00:13:48.230 --> 00:13:51.620
- It was super exciting
because it was on my first day,

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:55.310
so I don't even know why I had the feeling

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:56.910
that I needed to do that.

00:13:56.910 --> 00:14:00.140
It was for Roberta Battaglia,
she's a 10-year-old girl.

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:04.300
She was amazing and you know
what, after I've been watching

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:06.610
the show, I still really think

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:09.623
that it was the perfect
choice, right guys?

00:14:10.822 --> 00:14:13.400
- This girl is super, super talented.

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:15.020
- Simon, I don't know if you know this,

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:19.560
'cause you spend a lot of time
in the UK, but Kelly Clarkson

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:22.270
is also a singer who
was discovered on a show

00:14:22.270 --> 00:14:23.317
not like on our--

00:14:24.370 --> 00:14:25.540
(laughs)

00:14:25.540 --> 00:14:27.542
- We can't talk about other shows!

00:14:27.542 --> 00:14:30.302
(laughs)

00:14:30.302 --> 00:14:32.203
- All I can say is whoever
was judging that year

00:14:32.203 --> 00:14:33.833
must have been amazing.

00:14:33.833 --> 00:14:35.660
(laughs)

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:36.980
- He nailed it, they nailed it.

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:38.720
All right, well speaking of judges.

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:40.340
In the judges' cuts episodes,

00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:43.180
you're together for the first
time, how great is that?

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:44.013
- Oh.

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:47.590
- You know what, we're going
into unknown territory here,

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:52.590
Kelly, so this is I swear when
I say we are makin' this up

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:55.970
day by day, we are making
this up day by day.

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:58.730
But I've gotta hand it to
everyone on the call here,

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:03.300
everyone's embraced it,
everyone's contributed ideas.

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:05.450
Number one priority, keep safe.

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:08.673
Second priority, get the
contestants to be amazing.

00:15:08.673 --> 00:15:09.593
Third, have fun.

